  "about": "Conformance cases for the salted reference of a copy (specs/attestation/README.md §2.4a–§2.4b, RW-15). A copy commits to its record under a fresh salt: the issuer signs `_sd`, a list of `b64u(SHA-256(ASCII(disclosure)))`, and the holder keeps the disclosures, each `b64u(JSON([salt, name, value]))`. A reader is given a copy's `_sd` and the disclosures a holder presents, and must report: which disclosures are committed (their digest is in `_sd`) and which are not; the record hash a committed `record` disclosure opens to (64 lowercase hex characters, else nothing); and, when an artefact's hash is offered, whether the opened record names it (`opens`), null when no record was opened or no artefact was offered. Every salt and every decoy preimage is written here, so every digest is recomputable; nothing is signed and nothing here is a key. Reference implementation: @kashscript/attest/attestation's openRecordCommitment.",
